Add DELL0A86 to the existing ACPI 100 kHz I2C quirk table.

The ELAN 04F3:3185 touchpad exposed as DELL0A86 on the Dell Inspiron
13 5310 intermittently exhibits excessive smoothing when its I2C bus
runs at 400 kHz. During an affected period pointer movement becomes
severely sluggish and sticky for tens of seconds.

The ACPI firmware configures this touchpad bus for 400 kHz. Forcing the
bus to 100 kHz, as for other touchpads in this workaround class, stopped
the problem during extended heavy use and an S4 hibernate/resume cycle.

---
diff --git a/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-acpi.c b/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-acpi.c
--- a/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-acpi.c
@@ -372,5 +372,6 @@ static const struct acpi_device_id i2c_acpi_force_100khz_device_ids[] = {
	 */
+	{ "DELL0A86", 0 },
	{ "DLL0945", 0 },
	{ "ELAN06FA", 0 },
	{}
 };
